+# RE Mesh Editor workspace guide
+
+## Key Files
+| File | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `__init__.py` | Blender add-on registration, game enums and import/export operators |
+| `translations.py` | Blender `zh_HANS`/`zh_CN` UI dictionary and translation lifecycle helpers |
+| `LOCALIZATION.md` | Short guide for enabling and maintaining the Chinese localization |
+| `README.md` | Upstream documentation |
+| `.gitignore` | Excludes generated texture and updater caches |
+
+## Subdirectories
+| Directory | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `modules` | Mesh, material, texture, skeleton and Blender conversion implementations |
+| `docs` | User-facing workflow guides |
+| `tests` | Automated export-manifest regressions |
+
+## Dependencies
+- OWOTS adaptation baseline: upstream commit `622daa75b41ec622c3444ecb44ef31a651692687` (0.66).
+- Test against Blender 5.2, together with the sibling RE-Asset-Library-cn and RE-Chain-Editor-main projects.
+- The upstream bundled texture conversion and compression libraries remain required; do not omit them from installation packages.
+
+## Common Patterns
+- Workspace incremental exports share `capture_baseline`, `plan_export` and `execute_export`; selected owners update without dropping other collections from the Mod. See `modules/workspace/AGENTS.md` for persistence, conversion and publication rules.
+- Both workspace export buttons expand only selected Outliner collections into model assets. Present one model per row and resolve MDF/TEX dependencies without individual MDF selection; never fall back to all scene assets.
+- `OWOTS` uses mesh file version `260209350`, internal version `250203152`, six weights per vertex, and no extended weight buffer.
+- MDF 51 has a distinct OWOTS material header. Full, fast and write paths must agree; ordinary MDF 51 must remain readable.
+- OWOTS MDF import stores opaque material uints and file-header flags as custom properties. Export must preserve them; legacy scenes recover only metadata by material name from the original MDF baseline, and missing metadata must fail rather than write zeros.
+- TEX `251111100` is shared with MHS3. Distinguish the actual payload layout, not just the extension.
+- Prefer the real `streaming` texture when available. Base textures can be 256 square while their high-resolution counterparts are 2048 square; successful conversion alone is not a quality check.
+- Workspace TEX conversion takes color/compression semantics from original game metadata; Blender image color tags must not alter authored channels. Nullify Texture Bindings operates on each selected MDF object and reports unmapped types; it changes MDF paths, not viewport shaders.
+- Mesh export discovers used vertex groups in one pass per mesh, preserving zero-weight group membership semantics. Workspace dialog changes are lightweight; native DDS encoding runs in an isolated bundled-Python worker and must not crash the host.
+- The default mesh import should select LOD0. Test all-LOD imports separately rather than treating their combined vertex count as one high-resolution mesh.
+- `re_mesh.convert_to_empty_mesh` replaces selected editable meshes with tiny UV-mapped quads in object mode, preserving object identity/materials/armature links and shared unselected mesh data. It supports undo and binds skinned placeholders to a real bone with normalized weight; validate all targets before conversion.
+- UI localization lives in `translations.py`; keep English source strings, operator IDs, RNA property names, file formats and game identifiers unchanged. Register/unregister the table with the add-on lifecycle, and use the `Operator` context plus `pgettext_iface`/`pgettext_tip` helpers for formatted messages.
+- The updater treats `feat/onimusha-wots` as a manual-install branch target; only numeric fork releases/tags may set `update_ready` or report an automatic update.
+
+## For AI Agents
+- Keep changes on `feat/onimusha-wots`; `origin` is the user's `yequ172672/RE-Mesh-Editor-5.2-CN` fork and `upstream` is `NSACloud/RE-Mesh-Editor`.
+- Never commit TextureCache, updater runtime state, extracted game assets or user Blender preferences.
+- The primary repository distributes runtime changes as `compatibility/re-mesh-editor-owots.patch`; regenerate it after changes.
+- Coordinate live Blender MCP use through the primary agent; use isolated preferences for unattended tests.
+- Update relevant AGENTS.md files for structural changes and preserve manual marker sections.
+
+- Preserve upstream authorship and label yequ172672 as fork maintainer. Preferences and README link to `https://github.com/yequ172672/RE-Mesh-Editor-5.2-CN`; updater releases/tags use this fork and the explicit `feat/onimusha-wots` branch option. Do not fall back to upstream or the updater default master branch.
+
+- The N-sidebar RE Mesh tab includes a default-collapsed Fork Maintenance panel declared in `__init__.py`; keep it visible without an active object and respect the existing tab hide flag.
