new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d9108b0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/modules/workspace/AGENTS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# Mod workspace implementation
+
+## Key Files
+| File | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `re_mod_workspace_operators.py` | Existing workspace creation, porting and game file tracking |
+| `re_mod_workspace_propertyGroups.py` | Existing workspace and conversion settings |
+| `ui_re_mod_workspace_panels.py` | RE Mod Dev Tools sidebar, including both incremental export buttons |
+| `export_tracking.py` | Persistent source hashes, asset identities, material mappings and exporter-built baselines |
+| `export_handlers.py` | Save-pre packing of edited tracked images, preserving unsaved pixels across reopen |
+| `export_textures.py` | Image conflict resolution and temporary DDS-to-native-TEX conversion |
+| `texture_worker.py` | One-shot native DDS codec worker in Blender's bundled Python; process failures cannot terminate Blender |
+| `export_pipeline.py` | Selected-collection planning, dependency checks, conversion and PAK orchestration |
+| `export_manifest.py` | Blender-independent path validation, owner reconciliation and rollback-safe publication |
+| `export_operators.py` | Selected Outliner model discovery, dependency summaries and isolated legacy baseline recovery |
+| `mod_showcase_template.jpg` | Existing workspace showcase image |
+
+## Subdirectories
+| Directory | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `texturepacker` | Existing material porting and texture packing implementation |
+
+## Dependencies
+- Blender supplies bpy and NumPy. Existing bundled Texconv and TEX writers perform encoding.
+- Workspace encoding also requires Blender's bundled Python executable; subprocess output/errors stay inside staging. Ship texture_worker.py with the add-on.
+- RE Asset Library is optional for directory export, required for PAK creation.
+
+## Common Patterns
+- Capture the normalized game-export payload after import, not the edited state of a legacy scene. Never reset the import baseline after publication.
+- Reuse the Mesh/MDF export data builders for comparison and write the same bytes. Persist original source SHA-256 separately.
+- Mesh `_returnExportData` validation raises structured-detail errors without invoking the manual export error window. Import capture stores these as baseline errors; never treat a failed build as an unchanged mesh or modify weights to force a baseline.
+- Optional `force_mesh` skips mesh fingerprint comparison and permits stored mesh-validation baseline errors only. Retain source/game/path checks and current exporter validation; MDF/TEX remain incremental. Never reset or overwrite original baselines in force mode.
+- Independent `force_mdf` includes associated MDF regardless of its fingerprint and permits stored MDF-validation failures. When an old MDF ID is missing, associate only one same-parent/same-game/same-target-path replacement, remap material IDs in plan-only copies, and retire the missing owner in the manifest. Reject ambiguity; retain Mesh/MDF consistency, texture checks and original baseline records.
+- Collection, material and node identifiers survive renames. Copied identifiers are ambiguous and must fail explicitly.
+- MDF parameter callbacks may update preview nodes. Normalize only changes matching their authoritative MDF values; reject independent shader changes, including group constants.
+- A selection updates its manifest owners only; PAK includes all retained owners. Do not package arbitrary workspace files.
+- UI export scope is RE_MESH_COLLECTION descendants of selected Outliner collections, deduplicated and restricted to the current scene. Read selected_ids with both area and WINDOW region overrides; snapshot selection before opening the dialog. No selection must never mean all assets. MDF/TEX follow stored dependencies without separate checkboxes.
+- Stage conversions and PAK first, then publish with rollback. Respect external edits and never deploy to the game directory.
+- Run workspace Texconv in a one-shot bundled-Python process with COM initialized there; never load/unload the native encoder inside Blender for this workflow. Check exit status and output before TEX wrapping/publication. Compressed DDS inputs are rasterized to rebuild truncated mip chains.
+- Opening the export dialog and changing settings must never build meshes or hash textures. Full planning is explicit via Check Changes or performed once by execute; invalidate the optional summary on option changes.
+- TEX metadata owns output DXGI format/sRGB; preserve authored channels, save temporary pixel images as Non-Color and ignore source gamma through Texconv. Never change the original image colorspace (it can discard dirty buffers); Blender colorspace alone is not an export change. Game-channel conversion revision participates in cached output fingerprints.
+- OWOTS null-binding entries are verified against REE.PAK.Tool/Projects/OWOTS_STM_Release.list. Unmapped bindings must remain untouched; never substitute another game's unverified generic path.
+- A path-only edit to a known game default is MDF-only even when that TEX has not been extracted locally. Never synthesize old unchanged image data under the engine-default path. Count TEX files separately from edited images because streaming/base pairs create two files.
+- OWOTS scene-specific overrides cover 60 observed slots; see docs/owots-null-textures.md for individual rationale. Packed NRRC/NRRO/RCTO/STCM slots use named game defaults; gradients/noise/vector-field slots may retain general game resources. Presence in the list verifies the path, not shader-neutrality or in-game visuals.
+- Preserve physical streaming and base TEX paths. Arrays/HDR and unsupported graph edits fail rather than silently disappearing.
+- Both existing export dialogs expose `prefer_baseline_textures` (default false). When enabled, edited image pixels target their original TEX paths and streaming/base companions even if the MDF binding changed. MDF bindings and path-only edits remain untouched; this option must invalidate summaries without triggering planning.
+
+## For AI Agents
+- Test actual Blender operators and real source assets outside the repository. Headless tests must disable the existing showConsole preference.
+- Keep game assets and intermediate textures out of source packages. Sync the companion patch after runtime edits.
